 "narrative": "## The trajectory\nRevenue was $215.9B in FY2026 [1].\nRevenue CAGR was +46.6% over FY2017..FY2026 [2].\nNet income was $120.1B in FY2026 [3].\n\n## Growth quality\nRevenue growth in FY2026 was +65.5% [1] [4].\nNet income growth in FY2026 was +64.7% [3] [5].\nIn FY2026, net income growth of +64.7% [3] [5] was below revenue growth of +65.5% [1] [4].\n\n## Margins\nGross margin was 71.1% in FY2026 [6].\nOperating margin was 60.4% in FY2026 [7].\nOperating margin changed -2.0pp in FY2026 [7] [8].\n\n## Cash & balance sheet\nIn FY2026, free cash flow of $96.7B [9] was below net income of $120.1B [3].\nThe current ratio was 3.91\u00d7 in FY2026 [10], above 1.00\u00d7.\nIn FY2026, operating cash flow of $102.7B [11] was below net income of $120.1B [3].\n\n## Red flags\nRevenue YoY growth decelerated across its three most recent measurable observations: +125.9% \u2192 +114.2% \u2192 +65.5%. Source operands: Revenue USD 60,922,000,000 in FY2024 [12]; Revenue USD 26,974,000,000 in FY2023 [13]; Revenue USD 130,497,000,000 in FY2025 [4]; Revenue USD 215,938,000,000 in FY2026 [1].\nLong-term debt grew +276.7% from FY2017 to FY2026. Source operands: Long-term debt USD 1,983,000,000 in FY2017 [14]; Long-term debt USD 7,469,000,000 in FY2026 [15].\n\n## What to watch next\nWatch whether revenue growth in the next reporting update improves from +65.5% in FY2026 [1] [4].\nWatch how operating margin in the next reporting update compares with 60.4% in FY2026 [7].\nWatch how free cash flow in the next reporting update compares with $96.7B in FY2026 [9].",
